  "urpx:hasRatePlan": {
    "@type": "urpx:RatePlan",
    "@id": "smud:tod-5-8pm",
    "urpx:name": "Residential Time-of-Day (5-8 p.m.) Rate",
    "urpx:ratePlanUniqueIdentifier": "TOD-5-8PM",
    "urpx:initialEffectiveDate": "2018-10-01",
    "urpx:timezoneIdentifier": "America/Los_Angeles",
    "urpx:hasRatePlanVersion": {
      "@type": "urpx:RatePlanVersion",
      "@id": "smud:tod-5-8pm-2026-01-01",
      "urpx:description": "SMUD's default residential pricing plan — the standard TOU rate for ~85% of SMUD residential customers (~505K of 593K). Regulatory rate category RT02 within Rate Schedule R-TOD (which covers RT02 / RTL1 Low Use / RTC1 CPP under one Board-adopted resolution). 5-8pm peak window — distinctively earlier than the CPUC IOU standard (4-9pm) and reflects SMUD's independent rate design predating CPUC TOU mass migration. Filing source is SMUD's R-TOD schedule PDF adopted by Board Resolution No. 25-06-15 on June 19, 2025; the same resolution pre-publishes three forward effective dates (May 1, 2025 / January 1, 2026 / January 1, 2027) — this filing captures the January 1, 2026 column (current as of 2026-04-30 retrieval). Three TOU periods in summer (Peak weekdays 5-8pm; Mid-Peak weekdays 12pm-12am except 5-8pm; Off-Peak all other hours including weekends/holidays) but only two periods in winter (Peak weekdays 5-8pm; Off-Peak all other hours including weekends/holidays — no Mid-Peak in winter). Off-peak applies on 11 federal holidays (full list in source PDF Section V.A). Bill structure: System Infrastructure Fixed Charge $27.00/meter/month + Electricity Usage Charges per period. SMUD is a vertically integrated municipal utility (no CPUC PCIA/CCA split, no separate generation/delivery breakdown). Customers with NEM1 or SSR generation facilities approved on/after January 1, 2018 are MANDATORILY enrolled in R-TOD (not modeled as a separate eligibility gate; documented here for traceability). Plug-In Electric Vehicle Credit (-$0.0150/kWh, midnight-6am daily) modeled separately as a RatePlanModifier in grid-coordination/urpx-rate-plans#15 (secondary epic). Customer-generation overlays (NEM1, SSR), Hydro Generation Adjustment (HGA), Standby Service Charge, Three-Phase Service fee, and SMUD Renewable Energy Option also deferred to grid-coordination/urpx-rate-plans#15 or future modeling issues. Energy Assistance Program Rate (EAPR) and Medical Equipment Discount Rate are program-overlay modifiers also tracked at grid-coordination/urpx-rate-plans#15.",
      "urpx:effectiveDateTime": "2026-01-01T00:00:00",
      "urpx:changeReason": {
        "@id": "urpx:rateCase"
      },
      "urpx:priceCurrency": "USD",
      "urpx:commodity": {
        "@id": "urpx:electricity"
      },
      "urpx:serviceRole": {
        "@id": "urpx:bundledServiceRole"
      },
      "urpx:customerChoice": {
        "@id": "urpx:voluntaryChoice"
      },
      "urpx:isDefault": true,
